          "page": 1,
          "text": "The image is a block diagram depicting a trigger system for synchronizing a rotor with laser and camera equipment. It features a horizontal sequence of rectangular boxes connected by arrows, illustrating a signal flow from left to right. The process begins with a 'Rotor' block, which feeds into a 'Phase shifter'. The signal then passes through a block containing mathematical symbols '÷ m', followed by a 'Sequencer' block labeled with '✕ n'. From the sequencer, two parallel arrows point to two separate destination blocks on the right: 'Laser' and 'Camera'. This diagram visually represents a logical control path where a rotor signal is conditioned and sequenced to trigger external devices.\n转子 激光 相机 触发系统 同步 相位偏移器 时序发生器 框图 信号流 分频 倍频\nrotor laser camera trigger system synchronization phase shifter sequencer block diagram signal flow frequency division frequency multiplication\nRotor, Phase shifter, ÷ m, Sequencer, ✕ n, Laser, Camera\nThe Rotor block connects to the Phase shifter.\nThe Phase shifter connects to the block labeled ÷ m.\nThe block labeled ÷ m connects to the Sequencer.\nThe Sequencer connects to both the Laser and Camera blocks.\nThe diagram illustrates a sequential signal flow from left to right.",
